    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJDQ9E2V7MF4XRKW0MQQC59X",
        "created_at": "2026-02-26T19:37:23.804Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\n\n**What**: When agents start a task that has a `plan_ref` field, they should automatically retrieve the plan to get implementation notes, algorithm details, and design context. Currently the task-work skill and task-work-loop workflow do not mention checking plan_ref. Plans are the intended home for rich implementation context rather than cramming it into task descriptions or notes.\n\n**Where**: \n- `templates/skills/task-work/SKILL.md` — Step 3 \"Start Task\" section (line 86-90) needs a substep: \"If task has plan_ref, run `kspec plan get @plan-ref` to read implementation notes\"\n- Task-work-loop workflow definition in `.kspec/` (the workflow YAML) — add the same step\n- `src/cli/commands/task.ts` — the `task get` output already shows `plan_ref` when present; the `task start` command could optionally print a hint like \"This task has a plan: run `kspec plan get @plan-ref` for implementation context\"\n\n**How**:\n1. Update `templates/skills/task-work/SKILL.md` step 3 to add: \"If `kspec task get @ref` shows a `plan_ref`, run `kspec plan get @plan-ref` to read implementation notes and design context before starting work.\"\n2. Update the task-work-loop workflow to include the same check in its automated flow\n3. Optionally enhance `kspec task start` in `src/cli/commands/task.ts` to print an info message when the started task has a non-null plan_ref\n4. Run `kspec agents generate` after template changes\n\n**Done when**:\n- The task-work skill documents checking plan_ref when starting tasks\n- The task-work-loop workflow includes plan context retrieval\n- Agents following the skill will automatically get plan context when a task has plan_ref\n- `kspec agents generate` produces updated kspec-agents.md",
